'' --emit-doc: one module's public API, from its interface text and the comments above each line:
'' a type with its documented members (not its private ones), an enum, a constant, overloads as
'' one item, a declaration documented at its definition, a generic, an exported macro; nothing
'' module-private and no interface namespace in it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.edoc/cache
'' CLEAN: build/.edoc
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 --emit-doc build/.edoc/out tests/modules/src/docmod/geo
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: # geo\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: geo: shapes and their areas
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: ### Shape\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: A shape: a kind and its size.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: | `as long sides` | how many sides; 0 for a circle |
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: | `as double size` | the length of a side, or the radius |
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: *(protected)*
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: Its perimeter, in units.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: ### Colour\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: | `RED` | the first |
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: ### MAX_SIDES\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: The area of a shape, in square units.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: Documented at its definition only.
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: ### Bigger\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: geo.Double2( x )
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: Doubles x: an exported macro.
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: Secret_
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: Hidden_
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: m_hidden
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: __tko_mod_
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.md :: if a > b
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/main.geo.html :: <h3 id="shape">
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/.parts/main.geo.json :: "chain":"main.geo"
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/.parts/main.geo.json :: "name":"Area","namespace":"","qualified":"geo.Area"
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.edoc/out/.parts/main.geo.json :: function Area overload ( byval n as double ) as double
